    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our premier start. **Gunnar Henderson** faces Colin Rea in a hitter-friendly park with a +16% park adjustment and an elite 14% platoon edge, making him a cornerstone for our runs and RBI production. The outfield trio of **Kyle Tucker** (77.20), **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), and **Andy Pages** (72.66) follow closely; all three benefit from favorable matchups against Gabriel Hughes and Jose Cabrera. With xERA figures exceeding 5.00 for both opposing starters, our outfielders are primed to capitalize on high-volume scoring opportunities. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also presents a strong play (74.56) as he exploits a soft matchup against Arrighetti, bolstered by a significant +9% SP skill advantage and a +14% platoon edge.\n\nThe tightest decision on today's board involved **Miguel Vargas**, whose 53.40 score made him the most difficult cut. While **Miguel Vargas** boasts an elite 0.406 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Bennett, his efficiency score fell just short of the primary utility options due to a lower raw base projection compared to the surging **Curtis Mead** (62.84). We opted to prioritize **Curtis Mead**\u2019s +10% platoon edge against Arrighetti to maximize our 5x5 leverage. Meanwhile, we are monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (43.98) closely; his start is necessitated by roster depth, but he faces a stiff challenge in Dylan Cease, who holds a significant -19% SP skill advantage over our hitter, effectively capping his expected output today. \n\nOwners should note that several slots are pending official confirmation, specifically **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Cole Carrigg**. While our projections utilize historical batting order assumptions, any deviation\u2014particularly if **Kyle Tucker** is moved down the lineup\u2014could necessitate a slight recalibration of his overall efficiency. Outside of the lineup risk, we are clear of any major weather disruptions, though **Heliot Ramos** remains a high-risk play against Cease and should be the first player watched for late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit scenarios should the game script turn sour early.",
